# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the threading tests; see the README's "Build and install".
#
# TensorStore hands a task to another worker through a work-stealing queue that publishes it with
# std::atomic_thread_fence (tensorstore/internal/container/single_producer_queue.h). ThreadSanitizer
# does not model a fence on its own, so it sees no ordering between the thread that queued a task and
# the one that ran it, and reports every object the task touches -- in TensorStore and in the absl it
# is built on -- as raced.
#
# Suppressed by the top frame only: a race whose racing access is in this library's own code is still
# reported, whatever TensorStore did further down. What this gives up is a race in which this library
# hands one TensorStore object to two threads and TensorStore is the first to touch it.
race_top:^tensorstore::
race_top:^absl::
# Where a queued task's body starts: the call into the type-erased function TensorStore queued. Its
# name begins with its return type, so it is matched without the anchor.
race_top:absl::internal_any_invocable::RemoteInvoker
